{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"###Plan\n\nWe need to find a pattern that relates $x$ to $y$.\n\nThe terms in pattern $y$ are $\\redE{?}$ times the terms in pattern $x$.\n\n$y = {\\redE{?}} \\times x$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Describe the relationship\n\nLet's try each pair of $x$- and $y$ values in the relationship.\n\n$\\begin{align}\ny \u0026= \\redE{{?}} \\times x\\\\\\\\\n\\blueE{1} \u0026= \\redE{{?}} \\times \\blueE{3}\\\\\\\\\n\\maroonE{3} \u0026= \\redE{{?}} \\times \\maroonE{9}\\\\\\\\\n\\purpleD{5} \u0026= \\redE{{?}} \\times \\purpleD{15}\n\\end{align}$\n\nWe see that $y$ is less than $x$, so we must be multiplying by a value less than $1$.  What value for $\\redE{?}$ makes all the equations true?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\\blueE{1} \u0026= \\redE{\\dfrac{1}{3}} \\times \\blueE{3}\\\\\\\\\n\\maroonE{3} \u0026= \\redE{\\dfrac{1}{3}} \\times \\maroonE{9}\\\\\\\\\n\\purpleD{5} \u0026= \\redE{\\dfrac{1}{3}} \\times \\purpleD{15}\\\\\\\\\ny \u0026= \\redE{\\dfrac{1}{3}} \\times x\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Answer\n\nSo the terms in pattern $y$ are $\\redE{\\dfrac{1}{3}}$ times the terms in pattern $x$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"The table uses the following two patterns.\n\nPattern $x$: Starting number: $3$, Rule: add $6$\n\nPattern $y$: Starting number: $1$, Rule: add $2$\n\n$x$ | $y$ \n:-: | :-: \n$3$ | $1$ \n$9$ | $3$ \n$15$ | $5$\n\n\n**The terms in pattern $y$ are [[☃ dropdown 1]] times the terms in pattern $x$.**","images":{},"widgets":{"dropdown 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"2","correct":false},{"content":"1/2","correct":false},{"content":"3","correct":false},{"content":"1/3","correct":true}],"placeholder":"","stat